    {
      "short": "Scale up",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "title": "Vertical scaling: a bigger box",
      "body": [
        "The quickest fix is <span class=\"term\">vertical scaling</span> (scaling up): move to a 16-vCPU machine with four times the memory. No code changes, no new moving parts — the app doesn't even notice.",
        "CPU drops back to about 30% and p95 returns to 130 ms. The bill goes from $140 to $560 a month: in the cloud, price grows roughly in step with size."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "warn",
        "text": "Resizing a cloud VM usually means stopping it. Without a second machine, that's a few minutes of downtime."
      },
      "changes": [
        "~ Web app 4 → 16 vCPU",
        "~ Cost $140 → $560 / month"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "rps": 1200,
        "p95": 130,
        "cost": 560,
        "survive": "no"
      },
