    {
      "short": "One basket",
      "chapter": "problem",
      "title": "All eggs, one basket",
      "body": [
        "Then, on a Saturday afternoon, the host machine suffers a hardware fault. With one server there is no partial outage: <b>everything</b> is down until a replacement boots and warms up.",
        "A lone machine is a <span class=\"term\">single point of failure</span>. Planned work hurts too — every OS patch or resize is downtime."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "warn",
        "text": "Bigger hardware fails just as often as small hardware — and takes more down with it."
      },
      "changes": [
        "~ Web app DOWN",
        "~ Every request fails"
