    {
      "short": "Scale out",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "title": "Horizontal scaling: more boxes",
      "body": [
        "<span class=\"term\">Horizontal scaling</span> (scaling out) spreads the load across several ordinary machines behind a load balancer. Four 16-vCPU servers cost the same as one 64-vCPU machine — $2,240 plus about $25 for the balancer.",
        "Need more? Add a fifth. There's no top rung, and capacity grows (or shrinks) in small steps as traffic changes."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "+ Load balancer",
        "~ One 64-vCPU box → four 16-vCPU boxes",
        "~ Survives losing a server: yes"
