    {
      "short": "Lose one",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "title": "Losing a server is now a shrug",
      "body": [
        "When app 3 fails, the balancer stops sending it traffic and the other three absorb its share — each goes from ~55% to ~75% busy. Shoppers see slightly slower pages, not an error page.",
        "This is why teams size for <span class=\"term\">N+1</span>: enough capacity that losing any one machine still leaves everyone below the latency knee."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "~ App 3 DOWN",
        "~ Others 55% → 75% busy"
