      "short": "Recap",
      "chapter": "recap",
      "title": "Bigger or more?",
      "body": [
        "<ul class=\"takeaways\"><li><b>Scale up</b>: simplest, no code changes — but has a ceiling, needs restarts, and stays a single point of failure.</li><li><b>Scale out</b>: no ceiling, survives failures, grows in small steps — but needs stateless servers and a load balancer.</li><li>Plan for N+1 so one failure doesn't overload the rest.</li><li>Scaling the app tier moves the bottleneck to the data tier.</li></ul>"
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "next",
        "text": "Next: the load balancer — the front door that makes “more” possible."
      },
